    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1955-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Completing the square, \\[ \\begin{aligned} 4x^2-12x-1 &=4\\left(x-\\frac32\\right)^2\\\\ &\\quad{}-10. \\end{aligned} \\] The squared term is nonnegative, so the minimum value is \\(-10,\\) attained at \\(x=\\frac{3}{2}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Complete the square in \\(4x^2-12x-1\\)",
        "Factor \\(4\\) from the quadratic terms before forming \\((x-\\frac{3}{2})^2\\)"
      ],
